# requires.psv -- what a program needs that the card cannot see for itself:
# a Microware module the DEPENDS scan and the cio star do not record, another
# program, or a shell.  name|requirement|where it is stated.  The card lists
# each requirement under Needs; a name may have several lines.  Every line
# comes from a document on the disk or a measurement -- never from a guess.
# The trap-module lines were measured with tools/probe_trap_needs.sh, which
# runs each program with the module withheld and reads the module it asks for.
# That sees what a program needs AT STARTUP: bm names math inside it and
# starts without it, so a program may still want a module later.
a2p|perl, to run the script it writes|SRC/perl4/README-OSK; tools/datatests/perl.cases
perl|a shell named by SHELL for system, backticks and piped opens (SYS/login sets ksh)|SRC/perl4/README-OSK
